WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.868
Welcome to Frog Bot. In the next few minutes you will see how to work with your own team of AI agents, right on your computer.

00:00:09.268 --> 00:00:16.137
The first time you open Frog Bot, it asks you to sign in. Click Create an account.

00:00:16.537 --> 00:00:26.729
Enter your name, your email, and a password of at least six characters. Then click Create account. Your team is private to your account.

00:00:27.129 --> 00:00:36.183
Next, paste your Claude or OpenAI API key, and click Start. Your key stays encrypted on your own computer.

00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:47.101
This is your team. Frog is your lead agent. Say hi, and tell it what you need, in plain words, like you would tell a coworker.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:01:03.763
To add a teammate, press the plus button, and choose New agent. Give it a name, a short role, and plain instructions for how it should help. Then click Create agent. Each agent gets its own memory and its own computer.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:14.166
Now put them in a group, so they can work together in front of you. Press plus, choose New group, name it, and pick who is in it.

00:01:15.425 --> 00:01:27.423
In a group, type at, and a name, to talk to one agent. Press Tab to finish the name. Here, we ask Frog to get Dog to transcribe a video.

00:01:27.823 --> 00:01:37.645
You see every step live. The glowing bubbles show who is working, and when Frog hands the job to Dog, the hand-off shows right in the chat.

00:01:38.045 --> 00:01:50.523
Anything that sends, posts, deletes, or runs a command asks you first. Even from another chat, a bar at the top shows who needs you, with the buttons right there.

00:01:50.923 --> 00:01:59.116
Back in the group, Dog reports that the job is done. The transcript is saved in the shared folder for the whole team.

00:01:59.516 --> 00:02:10.659
Under the message box, choose how free your agents are. Ask first, Auto, or Plan. Click the mode, or press Shift and Tab.

00:02:11.059 --> 00:02:19.638
In Plan mode, the agent only makes a plan. When you like it, click Run this plan, and it gets to work.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:32.510
Click the panel button to see an agent up close: its setup and brain, its files, and its own screen while it works. Close it with the X.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:45.033
Open Integrations, at the bottom left, to connect your apps. The browser is built in. For Slack, one button opens Slack with your app already filled in.

00:02:45.433 --> 00:02:55.800
The Logs tab shows everything that happened, with the date and time. And Settings is where you change your key, your team name, and how much to spend.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:02.994
Your name is at the bottom left. Click it to change your name and picture, or to sign out.

00:03:03.394 --> 00:03:13.367
Closing the window keeps Frog Bot working from the tray, while your computer is on. That is it. Now give your team its first job.
